# Facilities CSV Import Walkthrough

I have implemented the ability to import operational facilities from a CSV file.

## Changes
### Backend ([server.js](file:///C:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/server.js))
- Added `POST /api/facilities/import`: Accepts a JSON array of facility objects and performs a bulk insert transaction.
- Returns success/failure counts.

### Frontend ([manage-data.html](file:///C:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/public/manage-data.html))
- Added "Import CSV" button to the "Active Facilities" section.
- Added [importFacilitiesCSV](file:///C:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/public/manage-data.html#1312-1371) function:
    - Parses CSV file client-side.
    - expects headers: [Name](file:///C:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/public/manage-data.html#1411-1415), `Location`, `Description`, `Boundary Notes`.
    - Sends parsed data to the new backend endpoint.
    - Displays success/error toasts and refreshes the list.

## Verification
### automated Integration Test
Ran a PowerShell script to:
1.  Authenticate as a user.
2.  POST sample data to `/api/facilities/import`.
3.  Verified the API returned `success: 2`.

```powershell
Import Result:
message          success failed
-------          ------- ------
Import processed       2      0
```

## How to Test
1.  Navigate to **Manage Data > Facilities**.
2.  Click **Import CSV**.
3.  Select a CSV file with the following format (header required):
    ```csv
    Name,Location,Description,Boundary Notes
    Site A,Texas,Main Plant,Control
    Site B,Ohio,Warehouse,Equity
    ```
4.  Verify facilities appear in the list.
